--TEST--
a second `$_` on one right side of a `|>` is refused, and the help names the local — `rule:expressions/pipeline-hole-once`'s E0130
--FILE--
<?nvs
// rule:expressions/pipeline-substitution — exactly one hole is what makes the
// substitution total: no temporary and no double evaluation, so a second `$_`
// is a refusal rather than a second lowering.
int $n = -3;
echo $n |> Core\Str::format("%s%s", $_, $_), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0130]: `$_` may appear exactly once on the right side of a `|>`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
